{
  "response": "# Accessibility Design Review: BuggyCarousel\n\n**VERDICT: REVISE**\n\n**Overall Assessment**:  \nWhile the component uses native `<button>` elements and provides basic labels for the buttons, it implements less than half of the WAI-ARIA APG Carousel pattern. The active slide indicator communicates state exclusively through CSS classes, slide transitions provide zero programmatic feedback to assistive technology, and the container lacks carousel role and slide group semantics.\n\n---\n\n### Pre-commitment Predictions\n1. **Missing carousel landmark and slide grouping**: Expected absence of `role=\"region\"`, `aria-roledescription=\"carousel\"`, and slide group semantics (`role=\"group\"`, `aria-roledescription=\"slide\"`). *(Confirmed)*\n2. **Missing dynamic change communication**: Expected no `aria-live` region or focus management to announce slide transitions when navigating. *(Confirmed)*\n3. **Visual-only active indicator state**: Expected indicator buttons to lack `aria-current` or `aria-pressed`, relying solely on styling. *(Confirmed)*\n4. **Uninformative placeholder alt text**: Expected non-descriptive alt text that conveys position rather than image content. *(Confirmed)*\n5. **Division-by-zero runtime failure**: Expected unhandled zero-length images array leading to `NaN` in calculations. *(Confirmed)*\n\n---\n\n### Perspective Alarm Levels\n\n| Perspective | Alarm Level | Trigger Signal |\n|-------------|-------------|----------------|\n| Screen reader | **HIGH** | Missing live region announcements, visual-only active slide state, missing carousel/slide landmark semantics, placeholder alt text |\n| Keyboard-only | **MEDIUM** | Linear tab order across all slide indicators without roving tabindex or grouped controls |\n| Low vision | **MEDIUM** | Indicator button hit target sizing (`24x24` px minimum) and active indicator visual contrast |\n| Cognitive | **LOW** | Straightforward previous/next controls, but uninformative image descriptions reduce comprehension |\n| Vestibular & motion | **LOW** | No auto-rotation, infinite looping, or motion animations implemented |\n| Auditory access | **LOW** | No audio or video media present |\n| Environmental contrast | **MEDIUM** | Active indicator state contrast against inactive indicators and background |\n\n---\n\n### Critical Findings\n\n1. **Active slide indicator communicates state only visually**\n   - **Location**: `BuggyCarousel.jsx:38-46`\n   - **Code**:\n     ```jsx\n     <button\n       key={idx}\n       onClick={() => setCurrentIndex(idx)}\n       className={idx === currentIndex ? 'active' : ''}\n       aria-label={`Go to image ${idx + 1}`}\n     >\n     ```\n   - **User Group Impacted**: Screen reader users, braille display users.\n   - **WCAG / APG Citation**: WCAG 2.2 SC 4.1.2 (Name, Role, Value) & WAI-ARIA APG Carousel Pattern (Slide Picker Controls).\n   - **Confidence**: HIGH\n   - **Why this matters**: The active state is represented solely by `className=\"active\"`. A screen reader user navigating the slide indicators hears \"Go to image 1, button\", \"Go to image 2, button\" with no indication of which slide is currently displayed.\n   - **Fix**: Add `aria-current={idx === currentIndex ? 'true' : 'false'}` (or `aria-disabled=\"true\"` on the active slide button per APG if the active slide is non-navigable) to programmatically communicate selection:\n     ```jsx\n     <button\n       key={idx}\n       onClick={() => setCurrentIndex(idx)}\n       className={idx === currentIndex ? 'active' : ''}\n       aria-label={`Image ${idx + 1}`}\n       aria-current={idx === currentIndex ? 'true' : 'false'}\n     >\n     ```\n\n2. **Slide changes are silent to assistive technology (Missing live region / state notification)**\n   - **Location**: `BuggyCarousel.jsx:17-23`\n   - **Code**:\n     ```jsx\n     <div className=\"carousel-images\">\n       <img\n         src={images[currentIndex]}\n         alt={`Carousel image ${currentIndex + 1}`}\n       />\n     </div>\n     ```\n   - **User Group Impacted**: Screen reader users.\n   - **WCAG / APG Citation**: WCAG 2.2 SC 4.1.3 (Status Messages) & WAI-ARIA APG Carousel Pattern.\n   - **Confidence**: HIGH\n   - **Why this matters**: When a screen reader user activates the \"Next\" or \"Previous\" buttons, focus remains on the button and no announcement is triggered. Because the DOM updates outside the focused element without an `aria-live` region, the user receives no feedback that the image updated or what the new image is.\n   - **Fix**: Provide an `aria-live=\"polite\"` status region or wrapper that announces the slide update, or mark the slide container with `aria-live=\"polite\"` and `aria-atomic=\"true\"`:\n     ```jsx\n     <div\n       className=\"carousel-images\"\n       aria-live=\"polite\"\n       aria-atomic=\"true\"\n     >\n       <img\n         src={images[currentIndex]?.src || images[currentIndex]}\n         alt={images[currentIndex]?.alt || `Image ${currentIndex + 1} of ${images.length}`}\n       />\n     </div>\n     ```\n\n---\n\n### Major Findings\n\n1. **Missing carousel landmark and slide grouping semantics**\n   - **Location**: `BuggyCarousel.jsx:16` & `BuggyCarousel.jsx:17`\n   - **Code**:\n     ```jsx\n     <div className=\"carousel\">\n       <div className=\"carousel-images\">\n     ```\n   - **User Group Impacted**: Screen reader users.\n   - **WCAG / APG Citation**: WCAG 2.2 SC 1.3.1 (Info and Relationships) & WAI-ARIA APG Carousel Pattern.\n   - **Confidence**: HIGH\n   - **Why this matters**: Assistive technologies encounter generic `<div>` tags without context. Users cannot identify that this widget is an image carousel, cannot jump to it as a landmark region, and are not informed of the total number of slides.\n   - **Fix**: Add `role=\"region\"`, `aria-roledescription=\"carousel\"`, and an accessible name (`aria-label`) to the outer container. Enclose the slide in a container with `role=\"group\"`, `aria-roledescription=\"slide\"`, and `aria-label={`${currentIndex + 1} of ${images.length}`}`:\n     ```jsx\n     <section\n       className=\"carousel\"\n       role=\"region\"\n       aria-roledescription=\"carousel\"\n       aria-label=\"Featured Images\"\n     >\n       <div\n         className=\"carousel-images\"\n         role=\"group\"\n         aria-roledescription=\"slide\"\n         aria-label={`${currentIndex + 1} of ${images.length}`}\n         aria-live=\"polite\"\n       >\n     ```\n\n2. **Placeholder non-descriptive alt text**\n   - **Location**: `BuggyCarousel.jsx:20`\n   - **Code**:\n     ```jsx\n     alt={`Carousel image ${currentIndex + 1}`}\n     ```\n   - **User Group Impacted**: Screen reader users, users with low vision.\n   - **WCAG / APG Citation**: WCAG 2.2 SC 1.1.1 (Non-text Content).\n   - **Confidence**: HIGH\n   - **Why this matters**: Announcing \"Carousel image 1\" conveys no substantive information about the visual content. The index position belongs in the slide/carousel metadata (`aria-label=\"1 of N\"`), while `alt` must describe the image content itself.\n   - **Fix**: Accept image objects containing explicit descriptive alt text (`{ src, alt }`), defaulting to a descriptive fallback only when decorative or unavailable:\n     ```jsx\n     <img\n       src={images[currentIndex].src}\n       alt={images[currentIndex].alt}\n     />\n     ```\n\n---\n\n### Minor Findings\n\n1. **Empty array leads to `NaN` and broken UI**\n   - **Location**: `BuggyCarousel.jsx:7-13`, `BuggyCarousel.jsx:20`\n   - **Code**:\n     ```jsx\n     setCurrentIndex((currentIndex - 1 + images.length) % images.length);\n     ```\n   - **User Group Impacted**: All users.\n   - **WCAG / APG Citation**: WCAG 2.2 SC 4.1.2 (Name, Role, Value).\n   - **Confidence**: HIGH\n   - **Why this matters**: If `images` is empty (`[]`), `images.length` is `0`, causing modulo by zero which results in `NaN`. This produces `alt=\"Carousel image NaN\"`, broken image source, and non-functional buttons.\n   - **Fix**: Add a guard clause returning an empty state or disabling controls when `images.length === 0`.\n\n2. **Touch/pointer target size for indicators**\n   - **Location**: `BuggyCarousel.jsx:38-46`\n   - **User Group Impacted**: Low vision users, motor-impaired users on touch/pointer devices.\n   - **WCAG / APG Citation**: WCAG 2.2 SC 2.5.8 (Target Size - Minimum).\n   - **Confidence**: MEDIUM\n   - **Why this matters**: Unstyled numeric indicator buttons typically render below the 24\u00d724 CSS pixel minimum target size requirement without sufficient spacing.\n   - **Fix**: Ensure CSS defines a minimum interactive bounding box of at least 24\u00d724 CSS pixels (44\u00d744 recommended) for indicator buttons.\n\n---\n\n### Enhancements\n\n1. **Group indicator controls in an accessible list or tablist**:\n   Wrap indicator buttons inside an ordered list (`<ol>`) or a navigation container (`<nav aria-label=\"Carousel navigation\">` or `role=\"tablist\"` / `role=\"group\"` labeled `\"Choose slide to display\"`) so screen readers announce the number of available items.\n2. **Keyboard arrow key navigation**:\n   Support `ArrowLeft` and `ArrowRight` when focus is within the carousel container to cycle through slides.\n\n---\n\n### What's Missing\n\n1. **Slide count and position context**: Assistive technology users are not told how many slides exist without manually tabbing through all indicator buttons.\n2. **Non-visual status announcement on Next/Previous trigger**: Activating Previous/Next updates the screen without any feedback to screen reader users.\n3. **Empty state protection**: No fallback rendering when `images` array is empty or undefined.\n4. **Explicit image content descriptions**: Props schema only expects an array of strings (URLs) instead of objects with accessible textual descriptions.\n\n---\n\n### Multi-Perspective Notes\n\n- **Screen Reader User**: Disorienting experience. The carousel has no landmark role or label. Moving between slides produces no announcement. Navigating through the indicator buttons does not indicate which slide is currently active.\n- **Keyboard-Only User**: Functional via Tab and Enter/Space on native buttons, but lacks roving tabindex or shortcut keys. If there are 15 images, the user must press Tab through all 15 indicator buttons.\n- **Low Vision User**: If the active indicator is only styled with color (e.g., grey vs. light blue), it violates WCAG 1.4.1 (Use of Color). Target size must meet 24\u00d724 px minimum.\n- **Cognitive Accessibility**: Inability to identify how many total slides exist and lacking text descriptions makes tracking carousel context difficult.\n\n---\n\n### Verdict Justification\n\nThe component is rated **REVISE**.  \nWhile it avoids serious anti-patterns like `div role=\"button\"` (it uses native `<button>` elements) and provides basic button labels, it misses the defining requirements of the WAI-ARIA Carousel pattern:\n1. Active slide state is visual-only (`className=\"active\"` without `aria-current`).\n2. Slide updates produce no assistive technology announcements (missing live region / slide semantics).\n3. Image descriptions are purely generic placeholders (`alt=\"Carousel image N\"`).\n\nImplementing `role=\"region\"`, `role=\"group\"`, `aria-current`, `aria-live=\"polite\"`, and object-level `alt` text will bring the component to full compliance and justify an **ACCEPT** verdict.\n",
